# Qalam Studio — environment variables
#
# ── Database (optional for local/offline testing, required for cloud sync) ────────────────────────
# Works offline automatically! If DATABASE_URL is not set, Qalam Studio
# uses local storage so all templates, canvas features, and exports work instantly.
#
# When deploying to Vercel or running multi-user cloud sync:
# Connect any PostgreSQL server (Neon, Supabase, Vercel Postgres, Docker, etc.)
#
# RECOMMENDED · Neon (fastest serverless Postgres, 100% free tier):
#   1. Sign up at neon.tech
#   2. Create a project
#   3. Copy the pooled connection string:
#      postgresql://[user]:[password]@[endpoint].pooler.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
# RECOMMENDED · Supabase (free tier):
#   1. Create a project at supabase.com
#   2. Dashboard → Connect → copy URI (transaction pooler recommended)
#   3. Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password:
#      postgresql://postgres.[YOUR-PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-eu-central-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#
# Then run:  npm run db:setup   (applies migrations + seeds 110 templates in one command)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/qalamstudio

# ── AI provider (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Qalam Studio works without any AI provider (all design features work).
# When these are set, AI features (Magic Layers, Assistant, Magic Write,
# image generation/editing, translate, photo search) activate.
# Credentials are SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never exposed to the browser.
#
# ZAI_BASE_URL=https://your-provider.example/v1
# ZAI_API_KEY=your-key

# ── AI agents / MCP server (optional) ──────────────────────────
# CANVIX_MCP_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-secret
